<title>CHINA: China opens new port for foreign ships.</title>
<headline>China opens new port for foreign ships.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Changshu port in China's eastern province of Jiangsu has opened to foreign cargo ships, the People's Daily said on Monday.</p>
<p>The port boasts a Singaporean-invested wharf with one berth capable of handling a 35,000-tonne container ship, and two other multiple-use berths, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Another berth built by a Hong Kong investor could handle a 5,000-tonne vessel, it said, but gave no further details.</p>
</text>
